{"id": "sllama0007", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for fluorine is F. It' s a highly reactive gas and one of the most electro negative elements on the periodic table.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0015", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The sport that was introduced as an event in the 1 9 32 Olympics was ski jumping. It became a part of the Winter Olympic s and has been featured ever since, showing off the excitement of winter sports.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0023", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for lead is Pb. It comes from the Latin word plumbum, which was used to describe the metal and its compounds.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0031", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The battle that marked the end of the Napoleonic war s was the Battle of Water loo. It took place in 1815 and saw British forces led by the Duke of Wellington defeat Napoleon's army. This victory effectively ended Na poleon's rule and brought a close to the long conflict that had spanned decades.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 21, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0039", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The United States has won the most Olympic gold medals. They have been very successful across many different sports over time, leading the count with thousands of gold medal s throughout history.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0047", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The famous poem, \"The Raven,\" was written by Edgar Allan Po e. It's a classic of American literature and is known for its haunting rhythm and dark atmosphere.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0055", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A spider has eight legs. So, no, it does not have arms.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0063", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The player who scored the most goals in a single World Cup tournament is Miroslav K lec, with 1 5 goals across two tournaments. He scored seven in 1 98 2 and eight in 1 998.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0071", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are four noble truths. The first is that suffering exists. The second is the cause of suffering is desire. The third is that there's a way out of suffering, and the fourth is that you can follow this path to end suffering by following the Eightfold Path.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0079", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The person who won the most gold medals in a single Olympic s is Michael Phelps. He won eight gold medal s at the 200 8 Beijing Olympics and also set multiple world records during those games.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0087", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are about 6 0,000 miles of blood vessels in the human body. That' s enough to circle the Earth twice and a half.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0095", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Olympic Games have been held in Australia twice. The first was the 1 9 5 6 Summer Olympic s in Mel bourne, and the second was the 20 00 Summer Olympic s in Sydney. So, two times in total.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0103", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Maria Sharapova is a professional tennis player.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0111", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for potassium is K.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0119", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The driest place on Earth is the Atacama Desert in South America. It's so dry that parts of it have never seen rain for decades or even centuries. Some areas get almost no water at all, making it incredibly arid and extreme ly harsh for plant and animal life.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0127", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The ocean that lies between Africa and Europe is the Mediterranean Sea. It connects the Atlantic O cean to the southern part of Europe, bordering countries like Spain, Italy, Greece, and North Africa on its eastern side.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0135", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Jupiter is the largest planet in our solar system.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0143", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The athlete who has won the most Olympic medals in any single sport is Michael Phelps, the American swim mer. He won a total of 2 8 Olympic medal s across four different Olympic games. Of those, 2 3 were gold medal s, which is an incredible achievement. His success came from competing in events like the 4 x10 0 and 4x 200 meter freestyle re lays, as well as individual race s such as the 2 00 and 40 0 meter fre estyles. His record stands out not only for the number of medals but also for the consistency and dominance he showed over many years.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 36, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0151", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are five pillar s of faith in Islam. They are: Shahadah, Salat, Sa yyam, Zaka ah, and Hajj.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0159", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are nine exit s in a non agon.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0167", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The term for the study of organ isms is biology. Bi ology comes from the Greek words bios, meaning life, and logos, meaning study or knowledge. So it's the scientific study of living things, including plants, animals, microorganisms, and even their interactions with each other and their environment.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0175", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The youngest president of the United States was Theodore Roose velt. He became president when he was just 42 years old, which is pretty young compared to most president s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0183", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Cells produce energy through a process called cellular res piration. This process involves breaking down glucose, which is a type of sugar, to release energy in the form of adenosine triphosphate or ATP. The main steps include gly colysis, where glucose is broken down into pyruv ate; the Krebs cycle, which further breaks down pyru vate and produces energy-rich molecules like NADH and FADH2; and oxidative phos phorylation, which uses these molecules to generate ATP with the help of oxygen. All of this happens mainly in the mitochondria, often called the powerhouses of the cell.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0191", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The fastest land animal is the cheetah. It can run up to 70 miles per hour.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0199", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The largest blood vessel in the human body is called the aorta. It' s like a big pipe that carries oxygen- rich blood from your heart to all the other parts of your body.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0207", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": null, "no_speak": true, "answer_text": "", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 0, "carrier_ended": null}
